# Feature list 
Feature requirements and changes are described in this document.
  - Already it is a X.org compatible framework
  - Try to keep the same framework friendly/compatible with wayland (labwc) 
  - (How? Suggestions and discussions invited)

## Decided after releasing the version v1.4

### CHANGE 1  
- Openbox icon upgrade
  - main icon upgrade
  - taskbar wmclass support

### FEATURE 1 
- Openbox buttons size enlargement (without increasing titlebar height)
  - button height and width enlarge
  - click-hit area visible on hover
  - action_hover.svg or action_hover.xbm (action = min / mix / close)

### FEATURE 2 
- Right-click context menu for 'Open in terminal' in file manager
  - context manager is shown when clicked on empty area in file manager
  - File managers = Thunar / Nemo / PCManFM?
  - (inspired by Nautilus which already has this support)

### FEATURE 3 
- Right-click context menu for comparing files in file manager (via meld)
  - menu-entries = 'Compare' / 'Compare Later' / 'Compare with' 
  - menu items dynamically shown depending on pre-selection
  - zero selected file ==> No compare menu-item
  - one selected file  ==> 'Compare Later' and 'Compare to' available
  - two selected files ==> 'Compare' (mutually) and 'Compare to' to compare 
with previously selected 'Compare Later')
  - (inspired by Nautilus which already has this support via *nautilus-compare* 
package)

### FEATURE 4 
- Right-click context menu to 'Compress' files in file manager (via zip)
  - menu entry = 'Compress'
  - one or more selected files/folders ==> offer the context-menu 
  - decide compression algorithm (with subsequent an interactive dialogue box)
  - (inspired by Nautilus which already has this support)

### FEATURE 5 
- Tiling when pressed-to-edge

### FEATURE 6 
- Protocol for homogeneous theme (light/dark) support across GTK2/3/4 apps
  - put only two themes in openbox -- Mistral (dark) and Obworks (light)
  - theme change via *obconf* utility, which should affect all app themes (via 
hooks? to config files?)  
  
  
